# About page

The topical-event About page explains the purpose and scope of its parent event collection. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/frontend-templates/topical-events/about/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

For a household project, use this page only when background, responsibility or scope would overload the main project page. State what the work covers, what it excludes and how its current status is maintained. Keep operational controls on their established native pages.

## Structure and behaviour

Link back to the parent project and distinguish stable background from dated progress notes. Identify the document owner using an appropriate role rather than publishing unnecessary personal information. Use genuine dates for public documentation; label specimen dates as examples.

## Home Assistant boundary

This is not an assertion of government authority or a live project-management system. A small project may need only a short About section on the same page. Do not duplicate status text in two places unless they share the same source.

